# =============================================================================
#  secrets.local.env  -  settings for the forge_everything packwiz scripts
# =============================================================================
#
#  hi. hello. before you say anything:
#
#  no, we did not commit our actual keys. we know exactly what you thought when
#  you saw a file with "secrets" in the name sitting in a public repo. you felt
#  a little jolt. you started drafting the funniest reply of your entire life.
#  you were ALREADY typing "bro 💀". we respect the hustle. wrong file though.
#
#  this is the .example. it is the blank one. the one you fill in. the real
#  secrets.local.env is gitignored, has been gitignored, will remain gitignored,
#  and if it ever isn't, that's a bug report and not a bit.
#
#  the only thing actually exposed in here is our folder structure, and frankly?
#  it's giving organized. scroll down. read the comments. we documented this
#  thing like it was going on our performance review.
#
#  anyway.
#
#  Copy this file to secrets.local.env next to the scripts and edit. The real
#  file is NEVER committed - add it to .gitignore. This .example file, which
#  contains no secrets, is the one that belongs in git.
#
#  FORMAT
#    KEY=VALUE, one per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#    Do NOT quote paths that contain spaces - the whole rest of the line is the
#    value, so "C:\...\NeoForge 1.21.1" works fine unquoted. (Quotes are
#    stripped if you use a matching pair, so quoting is harmless, just noisy.)
#    'export KEY=VALUE' is tolerated if you share this file with a bash setup.
#
#  RESOLUTION ORDER, per setting, first hit wins:
#    1. the -Parameter you typed on the command line
#    2. a real process environment variable of the same name
#    3. the key in this file
#    4. the script's built-in default
#
#  RELATIVE PATHS here resolve against THIS FILE'S folder, not your current
#  directory, so the scripts behave the same wherever you run them from.
#
#  ${VAR} REFERENCES expand against keys defined ABOVE them in this file.
#  Only the braced form expands, and never in *_KEY / *_TOKEN / *_SECRET /
#  *_PASSWORD values - a bcrypt CurseForge key is literally $2a$10$... and must
#  survive untouched.
#
#  You can point at a different settings file with -SecretsFile, or by setting
#  the FORGE_EVERYTHING_SECRETS environment variable.
# =============================================================================


# ------------------------------- Roots ---------------------------------------
# Set these four and most of the rest derives from them.

# The projects folder: proprietary mods folder, modpacks folder, other projects folders.
#PROJECT_ROOT=C:\Users\Terra\projects

# Modpack projects folder: modpack repos (Not the same as MODPACK_ROOT,
# which is the modpack repos with their packwiz inside of that).
# This is where you keep your modpack repos if you maintain multiple modpacks.
#MODPACK_PROJECTS_ROOT=C:\Users\Terra\projects\Minecraft Modpacks

# The pack repo: packwiz folder, links file, reports.
#MODPACK_ROOT=C:\Users\Terra\projects\Minecraft Modpacks\forge_everything

# The playable instance. INSTANCE_*_FOLDER keys below default to the
# conventional subfolders of this, so you usually only need this one line.
#INSTANCE_ROOT=C:\Users\Terra\AppData\Roaming\ModrinthApp\profiles\Forge Everything


# ---------------------------- Instance folders -------------------------------
# All optional. Uncomment only to override the INSTANCE_ROOT-derived default.
# Used by: Get-InstanceFileList, Get-ModFolderInventory, Resolve-InstanceByHash,
#          Build-CurseforgeEntries

#INSTANCE_MODS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\mods
#INSTANCE_RESOURCEPACKS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\resourcepacks
#INSTANCE_SHADERPACKS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\shaderpacks
#INSTANCE_DATAPACKS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\datapacks
#INSTANCE_PLUGINS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\plugins

# Paxi's datapack folder. Export-TagInventory reads this to find
# forgeeverything_datapack. If Paxi ever moves house, this is the one line to
# change - the script also probes config\paxi\datapacks, openloader\data and
# global_packs\required_data as a fallback, but only this key is authoritative.
#INSTANCE_PAXI_DATAPACKS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\paxi\datapacks

# The KubeJS folder. Only read when Export-TagInventory is run with
# -IncludeKubeJS, since kubejs\data tags are ours and usually not the problem.
#INSTANCE_KUBEJS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\kubejs

# ProbeJS dump folder. Get-CookedTags reads @special\types\index.d.ts from here
# to build the runtime tag index. Without it, every c:/minecraft:/neoforge:
# reference is unresolvable and the triage is mostly guesswork.
#PROBE_DIR=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\.probe

# The client log Get-CookedTags parses the "Mod List:" block out of.
#CLIENT_LOG=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\logs\latest.log


# ------------------------------- Pack + server -------------------------------

# Folder containing pack.toml. Used by Resolve-InstanceByHash -Apply,
# Build-CurseforgeEntries -Apply, and Set-ModSides.
#PACK_DIR=${MODPACK_ROOT}\packwiz

# The working server's mods folder - the sole source of truth for Set-ModSides.
# A UNC path is fine.
#SERVER_MODS_FOLDER=${MODPACK_PROJECTS_ROOT}\forge_everything_server\mods

# Alternative to SERVER_MODS_FOLDER when the server is remote and all you have
# is `ls` output: a text file with one jar filename per line. If both are set,
# the file list wins.
#SERVER_FILE_LIST=${MODPACK_ROOT}\server-mods.txt

# Optional for Set-ModSides. Only adds one distinction: a mod on the server but
# not on the client can be marked `server` instead of `both`. Leave unset
# unless you specifically want that.
#CLIENT_MODS_FOLDER=${INSTANCE_ROOT}\mods


# --------------------------------- Outputs -----------------------------------

# Where generated CSVs and reports go. Created if missing. Leave unset to write
# into the current directory, which is the old behaviour.
#OUTPUT_DIR=${MODPACK_ROOT}\reports

# Individual overrides. Each defaults to OUTPUT_DIR\<the filename shown>, or to
# .\<the filename shown> when OUTPUT_DIR is unset.
#INVENTORY_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\mod-folder-inventory.csv
#INSTANCE_FILE_LIST_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\instance-file-list.csv
#RESOLUTION_REPORT_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\hash-resolution-report.csv
#RESOLVED_LINKS_OUT=${OUTPUT_DIR}\links_to_mods.resolved-by-hash.txt
#DRIFT_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\links-drift-report.csv
#CURSEFORGE_WORKSHEET_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\curseforge-worksheet.csv

# Export-TagInventory writes a whole folder rather than one file: tags_raw,
# tag_entries, tags_merged, dangling_tag_refs, unknown_namespace_entries,
# declaring_conflicts, parse_errors, tags_master.json and summary.txt.
# Defaults to OUTPUT_DIR\tag_audit.
#TAG_AUDIT_DIR=${OUTPUT_DIR}\tag_audit

# Get-CookedTags writes cooked_tags.csv, tag_triage_all.csv and
# cooked_summary.txt here.
# Defaults to OUTPUT_DIR\cooked.
#COOKED_TAGS_DIR=${OUTPUT_DIR}\cooked

# Find-OreDuplicates input: the ore item scan CSV it classifies.
#ORE_SCAN_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\ore_item_scan.csv

# Find-OreDuplicates outputs. Each defaults to OUTPUT_DIR\<the filename shown>.
#ORE_DUPLICATES_DETAIL_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\ore_duplicates_detail.csv
#ORE_DUPLICATES_SUMMARY_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\ore_duplicates_summary.csv
#ORE_CLASSIFIED_ALL_CSV=${OUTPUT_DIR}\ore_classified_all.csv

# Where Ore_Duplicate_Report.md lands. Point this at the vault and the report
# drops in with its [[wikilinks]] already resolving, instead of sitting in a
# reports folder being technically correct and completely unread.
#OBSIDIAN_VAULT_DIR=${PROJECT_ROOT}\Obsidian\Forge Everything

# Overrides OBSIDIAN_VAULT_DIR for this one file, if the report belongs
# somewhere other than the vault root.
#ORE_DUPLICATE_REPORT_MD=${OBSIDIAN_VAULT_DIR}\Ore_Duplicate_Report.md

# The hand-collected links file, read by Resolve-InstanceByHash (drift report)
# and Build-CurseforgeEntries (free file-ids).
#LINKS_FILE=${MODPACK_ROOT}\links_to_mods.txt

# Where Resolve-InstanceByHash keeps its CurseForge rate-limit ledger and
# response cache (.cf-ratelimit.json, .cf-cache.json). Defaults to the script
# folder. Point it somewhere gitignored if you would rather these not sit next
# to the scripts.
#CF_STATE_DIR=${MODPACK_ROOT}\.cfstate


# -------------------------------- Versioning ---------------------------------

# A value YOU bump by hand, not a timestamp. Bump it whenever the mods folder
# changes in a way that matters. Get-ModFolderInventory stamps it into the
# inventory so consumers can tell stale data from current.
#
# leave it commented and every inventory gets stamped "unversioned", which is
# fine right up until you're staring at two CSVs at 2am trying to remember
# which one was before the Mekanism update. ask us how we know.
#MODPACK_VERSION=v0.0.1-Alpha


# --------------------------------- Secrets -----------------------------------
#  
#  the main event. the reason the real version of this file never touches git.
#  everything below is commented out and says "replace-me" because that is what
#  a template looks like. if you are still here going "yeah but what if" -
#  bestie. look at it. it says replace-me.
#
#  if either of these lines ever shows up in the repo containing a real value,
#  that is not a prank, that is an incident, and we would genuinely rather hear
#  about it from you than from a rate-limit ban.

# CurseForge Profile key
# starts with cfc_pat_. Paste it raw - no quotes needed
#CF_PROFILE_KEY=replace-me

# CurseForge API key from https://console.curseforge.com. Bcrypt format,
# starts with $2a$ or $2b$. Paste it raw - no quotes needed, and no ${}
# expansion is applied to *_KEY values, so the dollar signs are safe.
# (yes we tested that. the dollar signs used to eat the key. it was a whole
# thing. we don't talk about it.)
#CF_API_KEY=replace-me

# Optional. Modrinth requests work unauthenticated; a token raises rate limits.
#MODRINTH_TOKEN=replace-me

